WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.900
Connect your external agent to a released EigenVista window using the setup

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:10.280
instructions. Give it the session note and ask it to protect unsaved work.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:14.920
Open the supplied water calculation in the approved input folder. Check the

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:19.008
three atoms and twenty-four imported orbitals before choosing a field.

00:00:19.458 --> 00:00:25.170
Ask the agent to read the energies and occupations in the source. For this

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:30.066
closed-shell example, the highest occupied orbital is MO five and the lowest

00:00:30.066 --> 00:00:34.962
zero-occupation orbital is MO six. Use the returned field identity in the

00:00:34.962 --> 00:00:35.778
subsequent requests.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:40.580
Ask for the sampled raycast preview and then the volume preview at sixty-four

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:46.810
samples per axis. Keep the same camera and field. After each change, have the

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:51.370
agent read back the display state. These sampled views let you decide whether

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:53.061
to calculate a persistent mesh.

00:00:53.542 --> 00:00:58.963
Generate the signed pair at plus and minus zero point zero three. Ask the

00:00:58.963 --> 00:01:04.384
agent to wait for success, report the two mesh counts, and verify the exported

00:01:04.384 --> 00:01:09.418
PNG includes the signed field key. If a calculation needs to stop, identify

00:01:09.418 --> 00:01:13.677
that job specifically and confirm the prior completed result is still

00:01:13.677 --> 00:01:14.065
available.

00:01:14.582 --> 00:01:19.062
Request a distance monitor for the oxygen and first hydrogen, then sample the

00:01:19.062 --> 00:01:24.402
same orbital along that segment. Check that the sixty-five rows include both

00:01:24.402 --> 00:01:29.262
endpoints. Compare the measured bond and profile length, and read the status

00:01:29.262 --> 00:01:32.483
and scalar unit columns before using the table elsewhere.

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:37.592
After saving the orbital result, use a fresh copy to compare an

00:01:37.592 --> 00:01:41.454
electron-density shell and a solvent-accessible surface. Ask the agent to

00:01:41.454 --> 00:01:46.475
apply a clipping shader to an identified shell and return the exact parameter

00:01:46.475 --> 00:01:48.019
values with the figure.

00:01:48.998 --> 00:01:53.878
Ask the agent to check that every output opens from the results folder. Keep

00:01:53.878 --> 00:01:58.368
the PNG and tables with the original calculation, the camera and shader

00:01:58.368 --> 00:02:03.608
settings, and the native file. For batch conversion, use the bundled converter

00:02:03.608 --> 00:02:06.259
and verify each converted file separately.
